Make the broken links table readable at any width. It now has three columns instead of five — the link type travels with the link as a badge, and the status code carries its description inline — so the link is no longer squeezed into a quarter of the table by the page title. On a phone, where the table stacks into blocks, every cell keeps its own label instead of leaving a stray list of column names at the top, and the pagination wraps rather than pushing the page into a horizontal scroll. The CSV button's icon is lined up with its label.
